<h2>DFP EXtractoR 1.0</h2>
<p>
  Multilayer OpenEXR sequences to ProRes and PNG, with Cryptomatte matte
  extraction and light-group export — and, from this build on, the app can
  update itself.
</p>
<p>
  Fixed in this build: an export longer than about fifty frames could freeze
  part-way through, and Stop could not reach it while it was stuck. Long
  sequences now run to the end, and Stop lands within a frame of the press.
</p>
<p>
  Press Stop a second time to give up the frame that's currently rendering: the
  export stops right away instead of waiting for a slow frame to finish, and the
  summary tells you exactly which frame it dropped. The export bar now shows how
  long the current frame has been going whenever it is running unusually slow,
  and a frame that stalls for good is failed automatically — with a folder you
  can retry — rather than hanging with nobody there.
</p>
<p>
  The job folder is now the document. A new job asks nothing until you first
  save or export; then it asks one question — where the job lives — and
  makes a folder of that name holding the job file, with the passes, mattes
  and AE script written beside it. Type over the job's name if you like, and
  choose in Options whether the output files follow the job's name or the
  render's. Exporting again into a job that already has outputs asks first.
  Open Recent lists jobs, a job opens by double-click in the Finder, and the
  window's title is the job's name. The command line is unchanged.
</p>
]]></description>
